import Callout from './Callout.astro';
---
<Callout>
  <p><b>Not for now if your back hurts.</b> This plan is written to follow later, once a doctor or physiotherapist has said that jumping is appropriate for you. It is a general training plan, not a back-pain rehabilitation program; use the phases in the <a href="/core/">back-safe core guide</a> for that.</p>
  <p><b>Stop and get urgent help</b> for new bladder or bowel changes, numbness around the genitals or anus, or weakness or numbness in both legs (<a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/back-pain/" rel="noopener">NHS guidance</a>).</p>
  <p><b>During any session:</b> stay at 2/10 discomfort or lower and no worse the next morning. Stop a set if landings turn loud or uncontrolled, or if anything feels sharp, pinching, or catching in the back, hip, knee, ankle, foot or Achilles.</p>
</Callout>
